  <becoming_a_combatant>
    <overview>
      <rule>A noncombatant may become a combatant accidentally through surviving difficult circumstances or deliberately through renewed training and adventuring.</rule>
    </overview>

    <procedure name="remove_noncombatant_penalties">
      <step order="1">Accumulate the required XP from adventuring, including war.</step>
      <step order="2">Expend that XP instead of applying it toward class advancement.</step>
      <step order="3">Remove noncombatant penalties cumulatively, in order, by level purchased off.</step>
    </procedure>

    <rules>
      <rule>A 1st level noncombatant becomes a combatant by accumulating and expending 100 XP from adventuring or war.</rule>
      <rule>The 100 XP spent to remove 1st level noncombatant penalties does not count toward advancement to 2nd level.</rule>
      <rule>At higher levels, each level's noncombatant penalty removal must be purchased in order, cumulatively.</rule>
      <rule>Once a noncombatant begins adventuring to become a combatant, he can no longer accumulate XP in his character class until all noncombatant penalties have been removed.</rule>
      <rule>The character may abandon the effort at any time.</rule>
      <rule>If the effort is abandoned, the character reverts to noncombatant status.</rule>
      <rule>Returned penalties come back at a rate of 1 point per week.</rule>
    </rules>

